Z||000000||N_Man||07-01-2000||12:39 AM||||Started her up for the first time in 7 weeks today  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>After rebuilding the engine and all the labour myself,  Turned the key...nothing.  Checked the battery turned the key and after a bit of fussing she came to life.  Could barly hear the engine over a rattling heat shield but it was running.  (I did fix the heat shield)<P>The clutch pedal feels almost totally dead but im hoping it just needs the master cylinder replaced and to be bled(Master cylinder was leaking and the resoviure (sp) is pretty empty)<P>Once thats out of the way put the brakes and wheels back together and go  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000001||BN Boomer||07-01-2000||03:40 AM||||I know exactly how you feel! I've had my 85 GT for almost 3 months now and today was the first time I've heard her run! Finally finished up the engine swap and got her going. Had a few problems at first, but got everything sorted out and she's running pretty good. I took her out for a little cruisin', popped the sunroof out and let the wind blow through my hair, and it felt great. I still have to do a little more fine tuning, but this feels great!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
